{"schema": "l4/s1-calibration@2", "kind": "item", "item_key": "ce4ff11afdcc44a61bbc8bab91b3ff5b", "unit": "openspec:add-three-for-two", "unit_hash": "e093fdb6f6b381182cda1c8f59e1456bba93cfed4ef52575db6250740176f0b1", "project": "git-35b5a131ecf1", "run_id": "r-20261008T1703Z-5b71", "round": 1, "origin": "live", "subject": "src/pricing/offers.py", "state": "Spec:\nChange: add-three-for-two\n\nWhat Changes:\n- Add `pricing.offers.three_for_two(unit_price, quantity)`, which returns the price of `quantity` units when every\n  third unit is free. A negative `quantity` is refused with `ValueError`.\n\nImpact:\n`src/pricing/offers.py` (new), tests under `tests/`.\n\nNamed in the spec's design and tasks:\n- src/pricing/offers.py\n- tests\n- module pricing\n\nChanged file: src/pricing/offers.py\n\nChange:\n+from decimal import ROUND_HALF_UP, Decimal\n+\n+\n+def three_for_two(unit_price: Decimal, quantity: int) -> Decimal:\n+    if quantity < 0:\n+        raise ValueError(\"quantity must not be negative\")\n+    payable = quantity - quantity // 3\n+    return (unit_price * payable).quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)", "state_sha256": "1c73a0d16bb571c32586671f0d73a68116c1df6a3d308bdfcd7eb5329d8ee046", "question_set": "l4/file-relevant@1", "question_sha256": "8353d7dbdc8bba02a4ea8f2a6d4f36200219977e336d31bc83cea8f002a37af5", "expected": {"relevant": true, "unrelated": false, "relatedness": 2}, "label_source": "deterministic:scope", "tags": ["origin:live", "project:git-35b5a131ecf1"]}
{"schema": "l4/s1-calibration@2", "kind": "item", "item_key": "5a7fab7ee45e98092ad2fb08339002ea", "unit": "openspec:add-three-for-two", "unit_hash": "e093fdb6f6b381182cda1c8f59e1456bba93cfed4ef52575db6250740176f0b1", "project": "git-35b5a131ecf1", "run_id": "r-20261008T1703Z-5b71", "round": 1, "origin": "live", "subject": "tests/test_three_for_two.py", "state": "Spec:\nChange: add-three-for-two\n\nWhat Changes:\n- Add `pricing.offers.three_for_two(unit_price, quantity)`, which returns the price of `quantity` units when every\n  third unit is free. A negative `quantity` is refused with `ValueError`.\n\nImpact:\n`src/pricing/offers.py` (new), tests under `tests/`.\n\nNamed in the spec's design and tasks:\n- src/pricing/offers.py\n- tests\n- module pricing\n\nChanged file: tests/test_three_for_two.py\n\nChange:\n+from decimal import Decimal\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from pricing.offers import three_for_two\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.l4(\"C-86b721d4\")\n+def test_three_units_cost_two():\n+    assert three_for_two(Decimal(\"2.00\"), 3) == Decimal(\"4.00\")\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.l4(\"C-a172c4bb\")\n+def test_seven_units_cost_five():\n+    assert three_for_two(Decimal(\"2.00\"), 7) == Decimal(\"10.00\")\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.l4(\"C-29f9ec1e\")\n+def test_negative_quantity_is_refused():\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n+        three_for_two(Decimal(\"2.00\"), -1)", "state_sha256": "52cf7b9c97c444d668671c8a1cda1948e7df85b7f22d956670b9a801acd222c3", "question_set": "l4/file-relevant@1", "question_sha256": "8353d7dbdc8bba02a4ea8f2a6d4f36200219977e336d31bc83cea8f002a37af5", "expected": {"relevant": true, "unrelated": false}, "label_source": "deterministic:scope", "tags": ["origin:live", "project:git-35b5a131ecf1"]}
